---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How far should a backyard sauna be from a house or property line?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "There is no universal setback. Requirements can depend on local zoning, building and fire codes, easements, lot type, fuel source, sauna size, and HOA rules. Confirm the exact location with the local authority before ordering or building."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What makes a good backyard sauna location?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A strong candidate location is code-compliant, level or feasibly supported, well drained, accessible for delivery and maintenance, compatible with the electrical or chimney plan, and connected to the house by a safe, private path."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Base
  title="Best Location for a Backyard Sauna: A Site-Verification Guide"
  description="Choose a backyard sauna location by checking zoning, easements, drainage, foundation, power, delivery, privacy, weather, and service access."
  canonical="/guides/best-location-backyard-sauna"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Planning guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-4">Best Location for a Backyard Sauna: A Site-Verification Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm">Reviewed August 2026 | Verify requirements locally before ordering</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mt-4">The best-looking spot is not always buildable. Start with legal and utility constraints, then compare drainage, delivery, power, privacy, weather exposure, and the path you will actually use.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>No universal setback:</strong> Do not rely on a generic five-foot or ten-foot rule. Zoning, building code, fire rules, easements, HOA restrictions, fuel type, and the model itself can all change the required location.
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-stone-900">1. Draw the no-build areas first</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Use a property survey or reliable site plan to mark lot lines, easements, utilities, septic components, drainage routes, wells, protected trees, and existing structures. Then ask the local zoning or building authority what applies to the exact sauna size and fuel source.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">If an HOA or historic-district review applies, get written approval before purchasing. A retailer's general permit statement is not approval for your property.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-stone-900">2. Compare the remaining sites</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-10">
      {[
        ["Drainage and grade", "Prefer a location where water moves away from the foundation and door. Have the base designed for the soil, frost, runoff, and structure."],
        ["Electrical or chimney route", "Ask a qualified electrician or installer to compare service capacity, trenching, conductor route, disconnects, or chimney clearances before the layout is final."],
        ["Delivery access", "Verify freight dimensions, pallet weight, gate width, overhead obstacles, turning room, unloading equipment, and temporary storage."],
        ["Service clearance", "Keep all manufacturer-required clearances and enough practical access for exterior care, heater service, tightening, cleaning, and roof or snow work."],
        ["Privacy and path", "Plan a stable, lit, slip-resistant route between house and sauna. Screen views without blocking required clearances or ventilation."],
        ["Weather exposure", "Use site-specific wind, drifting snow, sun, tree debris, and runoff information. Do not assume one compass direction is best across North America."]
      ].map(([title, body]) => (
        <section class="bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">{title}</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">{body}</p>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-stone-900">3. Score each candidate before committing</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead><tr class="text-left border-b border-stone-300"><th class="py-3 pr-4">Check</th><th class="py-3 pr-4">Evidence to collect</th><th class="py-3">Pass?</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody class="text-stone-700">
          {[
            ["Legal placement", "Written setback, permit, easement, and HOA confirmation"],
            ["Foundation", "Site-specific base plan and drainage path"],
            ["Utilities", "Electrician or installer feasibility and quote"],
            ["Delivery", "Seller freight plan matched to the access route"],
            ["Maintenance", "Manufacturer clearances plus practical service access"],
            ["Daily use", "Private, lit, stable route and cooling area"]
          ].map(([check, evidence]) => <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">{check}</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">{evidence}</td><td class="py-3">[ ]</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-stone-900">Common expensive mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-stone-700 mb-8">
      <li>Ordering before confirming the legal footprint and easements.</li>
      <li>Pricing only the sauna while ignoring trenching, panel capacity, base work, freight, or a crane.</li>
      <li>Using a generic setback or wind-direction rule from another jurisdiction.</li>
      <li>Placing the door where roof runoff, drifting snow, mud, or ice collects.</li>
      <li>Leaving no access for exterior finishing, heater service, or warranty inspections.</li>
      <li>Assuming a freight truck can reach the final location.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="bg-stone-800 text-white rounded-xl p-6 mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">Turn the location into a project budget</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-300 mb-4">The same sauna can have a very different installed cost at two spots in the same yard.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/tools/sauna-cost-calculator/" class="inline-block bg-amber-400 hover:bg-amber-500 text-stone-900 font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg">Estimate the full project</a>
        <a href="/guides/outdoor-sauna-buying-checklist/" class="inline-block border border-stone-500 hover:border-stone-300 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg">Open the buying checklist</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
